@startuml actor-lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

title Actor Lifecycle State Machine

state "Initialized" as init : Actor created but not started\n(ready, done, stop channels allocated)
state "Started" as started : Processing messages from input channel\nBehaviorStack active, GoActorContext injected
state "Stopping" as stopping : Stop channel closed\nNo new messages accepted
state "Done" as done : Successfully stopped
state "StoppedWithError" as error : Stopped due to error
state "Cancelled" as cancelled : Context cancelled
state "Panicked" as panicked : Recovered from panic

[*] --> init : actor.New(opts...)\nor actor.StartNew()

init --> started : Start(ctx)\n[CheckState(Initialized) guard]
init --> error : Start() fails\n(e.g. provider missing)

started --> stopping : Stop()\n[atomic.CompareAndSwapUint64]\nclose(stop channel)
started --> cancelled : Context cancelled
started --> panicked : Panic recovered\n(catchPanic → OnError hook)
started --> error : Error during execution

stopping --> done : Graceful shutdown complete\nclose(done channel)
stopping --> error : Shutdown timeout
stopping --> cancelled : Context cancelled during stop

done --> [*]
error --> [*]
cancelled --> [*]
panicked --> [*]

note right of init
  **Channels allocated:**
  • input: bounded message queue
  • ready: closed when started
  • done: closed on termination
  • stop: closed to signal shutdown
end note

note right of started
  **Processing loop:**
  select {
    case msg := <-input:
      behavior.Current()(ctx, msg, entity)
    case <-stop:
      transition to Done
  }

  **Hooks:** BeforeStart, AfterStart
  **Middleware:** chain applied to handler
  **GoActorContext:** injected via context.WithValue
end note

note right of stopping
  **CAS-based Stop:**
  CompareAndSwap(Started → Stopping)
  ensures concurrent Stop() calls are safe

  **Hooks:** BeforeStop, AfterStop
end note

note bottom of error
  **Terminal state**
  Hooks: OnError
  done channel closed
end note

@enduml
